/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the functionality and use cases of `collections.defaultdict` compared to `dict.setdefault\(\)`.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   `collections.defaultdict` takes a factory callable \(such as `list`, `int`, `set`\) at) Tj
T*
(   initialization:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   from collections import defaultdict) Tj
T*
(   # Grouping elements by remainder modulo 3) Tj
T*
(   groups = defaultdict\(list\)) Tj
T*
(   for x in [10, 14, 21, 22, 27, 30]:) Tj
T*
(   groups[x % 3].append\(x\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Comparison with `dict.setdefault\(\)`:) Tj
T*
(   `dict.setdefault\(k, []\)` requires evaluating the default argument on every call, which creates) Tj
T*
(   a new list in memory even if the key already exists. `defaultdict` only invokes the factory) Tj
T*
(   function when a missing key is accessed, making it faster and cleaner for grouping operations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 9:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the behavior and advantages of `collections.deque` over standard Python lists for FIFO queue operations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   `collections.deque` is implemented as a doubly linked list of fixed-size blocks \(typically 64) Tj
T*
(   elements per block\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   - In a standard Python list, `pop\(0\)` or `insert\(0, v\)` requires shifting all N elements in) Tj
T*
(   contiguous memory, incurring O\(N\) linear time.) Tj
T*
(   - In `deque`, `appendleft\(\)` and `popleft\(\)` run in strictly O\(1\) time by adding or removing) Tj
T*
ET

