(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the mathematical set operations available in Python and demonstrate their syntax with bitwise operators.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Python sets support full mathematical set theory:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   - Union `A | B`: Elements in either A or B \(`A.union\(B\)`\).) Tj
T*
(   - Intersection `A & B`: Elements present in both A and B \(`A.intersection\(B\)`\).) Tj
T*
(   - Difference `A - B`: Elements in A that are not in B \(`A.difference\(B\)`\).) Tj
T*
(   - Symmetric Difference `A ^ B`: Elements in either A or B, but not both) Tj
T*
(   \(`A.symmetric_difference\(B\)`\).) Tj
T*
(   - Subset `A <= B` and Superset `A >= B`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Bitwise operators require both operands to be sets, whereas named methods can accept any) Tj
T*
(   iterable.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
