T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   `memoryview` is a built-in wrapper that exposes CPython's Buffer Protocol at the Python level.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   When slicing large binary datasets \(e.g. 100 MB of digitized ADC samples\):) Tj
T*
(   - Slicing a `bytes` object `data[1000:2000]` creates an entire copy of those 1000 bytes in a) Tj
T*
(   new memory allocation.) Tj
T*
(   - Creating a `mv = memoryview\(data\)` and slicing `mv[1000:2000]` allocates only a tiny 48-byte) Tj
T*
(   descriptor object pointing to the existing memory offset.) Tj
T*
(   - This provides zero-copy operations, dramatically saving RAM and reducing CPU memory bus) Tj
T*
(   bandwidth during high-frequency signal processing.) Tj
