(   [Problem Statement]: Implement an LRU \(Least Recently Used\) cache using `collections.OrderedDict` with full get and put operations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   An LRU cache evicts the least recently accessed item when capacity is reached:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   from collections import OrderedDict) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class LRUCache:) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, capacity: int\):) Tj
T*
(   self.capacity = capacity) Tj
T*
(   self.cache = OrderedDict\(\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def get\(self, key\):) Tj
T*
(   if key not in self.cache:) Tj
T*
(   return -1) Tj
T*
(   # Mark as recently used by moving to end) Tj
T*
(   self.cache.move_to_end\(key\)) Tj
T*
(   return self.cache[key]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def put\(self, key, value\):) Tj
T*
(   if key in self.cache:) Tj
T*
(   self.cache.move_to_end\(key\)) Tj
T*
(   self.cache[key] = value) Tj
T*
(   if len\(self.cache\) > self.capacity:) Tj
T*
(   # Pop oldest element \(FIFO from front\)) Tj
T*
(   self.cache.popitem\(last=False\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
