(   [Problem Statement]: Explain memory optimization using `__slots__` in Python classes with memory profiling comparisons.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   By default, every Python instance stores attributes in an internal dictionary `__dict__`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   - A default instance dictionary consumes ~150 to 200 bytes per instance even for just 2) Tj
T*
(   attributes.) Tj
T*
(   - Specifying `__slots__ = \('x', 'y'\)` instructs CPython to replace `__dict__` with a compact) Tj
T*
(   array of C pointers directly in the instance struct.) Tj
T*
(   - For 1,000,000 telemetry sensor records, using `__slots__` reduces memory consumption from) Tj
T*
(   ~180 MB down to ~45 MB, speeding up attribute access by ~20%.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
